    <string name="privacy_body">Usar keeps your history, saved websites, favorites and settings only on this device. Nothing is sent to us, there are no ads and no analytics.\n\nSigning in with Google is optional. If you sign in, only your name and e-mail are kept on this device; Google handles the sign-in itself.\n\nPasswords are never stored or logged by Usar. Websites can use your camera, microphone or location only after you allow it, and you can change that at any time in Site permissions.\n\nPrivate tabs use a separate storage area that is deleted when the last private tab closes (requires a recent Android System WebView).\n\nWeb pages are shown by Android System WebView, which is provided and updated by Google through Google Play. Safe Browsing protection in WebView may check addresses with Google.</string>
    <string name="privacy_heading">Your data stays on your device</string>
    <string name="privacy_info">Privacy information</string>
    <string name="private_body">Pages you visit in private tabs aren’t saved to history, and cookies and site data are deleted when you close all private tabs. Downloads and favorites you add are kept. Websites and your network can still see your activity.</string>
    <string name="private_not_isolated">Your Android System WebView is too old to keep private tabs separate. Cookies may be shared with normal tabs. Update WebView for full private browsing.</string>
